# PROVENANCE - nonfree/aic8800d80

AICSemi AIC8800D80 WiFi/Bluetooth firmware, for the StarFive VisionFive 2 Lite's onboard radio (SDIO,
DesignWare `dw_mmc` host at `0x16020000`, SDIO IDs `C8A1:0082` and `C8A1:0182`). `docs/wifi.md` section 44.

**Why this is here at all, and why it is not source.** Like the Pi 4's CYW43455, this part carries its own
processor and RAM, and the host uploads the program it runs - several patches and then `fmacfw`, the
full-MAC firmware. Nobody writes these but the vendor. See `docs/wifi.md` section 8.

**Licence.** Read `LICENCE` in this directory before anything else: these files have NO licence from
AICSemi. That file records the only written terms they travel under, what they do and do not mean, and
`docs/licensing.md` section 5a records that carrying them is an exception taken on the operator's decision
of 2026-10-04.

**Retrieved** 2026-10-04 from `radxa-pkg/aic8800`, commit `09c65d618f5ccde3233f8f41ef2f55b205ef11db`
("feat: update to aic8800d_linux_sdk_V4.0_2025_0410_b99ca8b6", 2025-07-22), path
`src/SDIO/driver_fw/fw/aic8800D80/`. **Not Radxa's current `main`:** at `main` (`d13d0796`, 2026-09-29)
four of the five files are a newer release. The commit above was chosen because it is the one whose files
match, byte for byte, what the board's own vendor image loaded - the VisionFive 2 Lite's StarFive Debian
boot log printed an MD5 for each file as its driver read it, and every one matches:

