The load order on the board was the order of this table: patch table, ADID, patch, extension patch, then,
after the Bluetooth patch-table pass, `fmacfw`. The SDIO clock was 5 MHz for the loads.

**To verify a copy**, fetch
`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/radxa-pkg/aic8800/09c65d618f5ccde3233f8f41ef2f55b205ef11db/src/SDIO/driver_fw/fw/aic8800D80/<file>`
and compare the SHA-256. Nothing here has to be trusted on this project's word.

**Not carried, deliberately.** The same directory upstream also holds `fmacfw_8800d80_u02_ipc.bin`,
`fmacfwbt_8800d80_u02.bin` and `lmacfw_rf_8800d80_u02.bin`. The board's vendor image did not load them, and
a blob nothing loads is a blob nobody can vouch for (26.2). They join this directory when a driver needs
one, with their own row here.
